Patch 37. In the series since 2026-10-17, after patch 36.

The 0xE0000000 physical heap starts 0x1000 into its physical range. Where the host's allocation
granularity is coarser than 4 KB the mapping rounds that away and guest accesses add 0x1000 back:
in recompiled code (REX_PHYS_HOST_OFFSET, a compile-time constant in the generated pch), in
GuestPtr (PhysicalHostOffset) and in the heap (host_address_offset, chosen at run time). Android
arm64 devices have 4 KB or 16 KB pages, known only at run time, and the SDK gave Android 0: a
16 KB device would read 4 KB off. Android arm64 now always takes the offset, as macOS arm64
does, so one build runs on both:

- PhysicalHostOffset (rex/system/xmemory.h) and REX_PHYS_HOST_OFFSET in the codegen and PPC test
  templates include REX_PLATFORM_ANDROID on arm64.
- PhysicalHeap::Initialize sets host_address_offset when the granularity is coarser than 4 KB, as
  before, or when PhysicalHostOffset asks for it; MapViews starts the 0xE0000000 view at the
  file offset that host_address_offset assumes (0x1000 lower) whatever the granularity.
- The generated pch asserts that its REX_PHYS_HOST_OFFSET equals PhysicalHostOffset, so code
  generated for another rule fails to build instead of running.

Desktop: the same offsets as before (Windows and macOS arm64 0x1000, Linux and macOS x86-64 0;
MapViews' file offsets are the same on Windows). The game's recompiled code from this rexglue is
byte for byte the same; only its pch changes (the condition and the assert).

Test: heap_allocation_test.cpp, on every platform: the 0xE0000000 heap's host_address_offset
equals PhysicalHostOffset, and a word written at GuestPtr(addr) is read at physical address
addr - 0xE0000000 + 0x1000, and back. On Linux, with PhysicalHostOffset forced to 0x1000
(Android's rule on 4 KB pages) all memory tests pass; with it forced but the heap and the views
unchanged this case fails (offset 0, the word not found). On devices: 4 KB and 16 KB through
tools/android/run_sdk_tests.sh. The game's cmake/guest_host_offset.cmake takes the same rule.

